Title: "Defines"
Id: "13d7dffc-b893-4883-8713-94f043308359"

Text: "```mlg-fragment
[CommandHeader]
Defines: <DefinesTargetUnion>
using?: <DeclarationStatement>+
when?: <ClauseUnion>+
extends?: <IsOrViaItemUnion>
declares?: <IsOrViaItemUnion>+
satisfies?: <ClauseUnion>+
Requires?: <RequiresItemUnion>+
Enables?: <EnablesItemUnion>+
Documented?: <DocumentedItemUnion>+
Justification?: <HaveGroup>+
Aliases?: <AliasItemUnion>+
Writing?: \"<WritingAlias>\"+
References?: <ResourceHeader>+
Metadata?: <MetadataItemUnion>+
Id?: <OpenText>
```

`Defines:` introduces a command as a mathematical form or a typed,
value-bearing declaration. Its target is tried first as a form/declaration and
then as an ordinary declaration statement, so both `Defines: G ::= (X, *, e)`
and `Defines: X := value is \set` are accepted.

```mlg-fragment
[\group]
Defines: G ::= (X, *, e)
extends: G is \set via X
declares:
. * is \function:on{X}:to{X}
. e \"in\" G
Documented:
. called: \"group\"
Id: \"23e4567e-e89b-42d3-a456-426614174000\"
```

Header parameters must be specified in `when:`. Symbols the target introduces
must be typed directly, through `extends:`, or through `declares:`.

`using:` introduces auxiliary symbols. `extends:` records the subtype or
extension view (see Via Keyword). `declares:` types the parts of the described
form, including the components of a destructuring target; those facts are
assumed while checking the body and are carried by values of the type.
`satisfies:` records the defining conditions.

`Requires:` and `Enables:` describe capabilities the checker can use when
resolving notation. `Documented:` must include at least one of `called:` or
`written:`. `Id:` is required for every top-level item; `mlg check` adds it when
missing.

Only `Defines:` has a `declares:` section, and only `Defines:` may use an
infix-specification heading such as `[A \:subset:/ B]`."
Id: "b2614ebb-ec03-4101-b137-fed2ef759073"
